[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907686483","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106789#issuecomment-2907686483","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106789","id":2907686483,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tT8ZT","user":{"login":"zimonitrome","id":17656709,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NjU2NzA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17656709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome","html_url":"https://github.com/zimonitrome","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-25T08:21:37Z","updated_at":"2025-05-25T08:21:37Z","body":"I'm guessing it's a floating-point error. Is it really a big problem?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907686483/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907937854","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106789#issuecomment-2907937854","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106789","id":2907937854,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tU5w-","user":{"login":"EdwardChanCH","id":97891482,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdW0mg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97891482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH","html_url":"https://github.com/EdwardChanCH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-25T16:46:46Z","updated_at":"2025-05-25T16:46:46Z","body":"Yes, it is a floating-point error. It is not a big problem, but any subsequent Basis.rotated() calls would require Vector3.normalized() on the basis's axis, which is avoidable if Basis.orthonormalized() works as consistently as Vector3.normalized().\n\n<img width=\"656\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b39a141b-7aeb-4bf2-91e4-d0c3e5bc688d\" />\n\n<img width=\"655\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d948124a-f6b9-443d-bea7-8c94273b94fc\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907937854/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2908277126","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106789#issuecomment-2908277126","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106789","id":2908277126,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tWMmG","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-26T01:38:30Z","updated_at":"2025-05-26T01:38:51Z","body":"I can also reproduce it in C#.\n\n>if Basis.orthonormalized() works as consistently as Vector3.normalized().\n\nThey should be consistent, Basis.orthonormalized() calls Vector3.normalized() internally. If you call Basis.orthonormalized() twice, the length is also exactly 1.0.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2908277126/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912004619","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106789#issuecomment-2912004619","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106789","id":2912004619,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tkaoL","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T10:27:54Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T10:28:18Z","body":"> I can also reproduce it in C#.\n> \n> > if Basis.orthonormalized() works as consistently as Vector3.normalized().\n> \n> They should be consistent, Basis.orthonormalized() calls Vector3.normalized() internally. If you call Basis.orthonormalized() twice, the length is also exactly 1.0.\n\nInteresting. I guess it should be possible to fix this by using `double` internally for the `normalize()` function, such that the floating point errors happen in the precision range that is discarded when converting back to float.\n\nThis might be somewhat slower though than on floats, since `SSE2` (our SIMD baseline on x64) and `NEON` (our SIMD baseline on arm64) can only divide 2 doubles at once, as opposed to 4 floats. \n\nStill, it might be worth it, depending on how big of a difference this performance difference makes practically. Someone would have to measure it.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912004619/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912411188","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106789#issuecomment-2912411188","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106789","id":2912411188,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tl940","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T12:54:15Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T12:54:15Z","body":"dotnet label seems not right. I think this issue is  floating-point error and not specific to dotnet.\n\n>Interesting. I guess it should be possible to fix this by using double internally for the normalize() function, such that the floating point errors happen in the precision range that is discarded when converting back to float.\n\nGodot supports double-precision builds.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912411188/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912464566","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106789#issuecomment-2912464566","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106789","id":2912464566,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tmK62","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T13:11:22Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T13:11:22Z","body":"> > Interesting. I guess it should be possible to fix this by using double internally for the normalize() function, such that the floating point errors happen in the precision range that is discarded when converting back to float.\n> \n> Godot supports double-precision builds.\n\nSure. That just means the bug may still occur in double precision builds, but shouldn't anymore in regular single precision builds.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912464566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2914825447","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106789#issuecomment-2914825447","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106789","id":2914825447,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tvLTn","user":{"login":"EdwardChanCH","id":97891482,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdW0mg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97891482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH","html_url":"https://github.com/EdwardChanCH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T03:56:13Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T03:56:13Z","body":"> Interesting. I guess it should be possible to fix this by using double internally for the normalize() function, such that the floating point errors happen in the precision range that is discarded when converting back to float.\n\n> They should be consistent, Basis.orthonormalized() calls Vector3.normalized() internally. If you call Basis.orthonormalized() twice, the length is also exactly 1.0.\n\nI'll see if I can fix `normalize()` this way. The `length()` function may also need this fix, since calling `orthonormalized()` twice still doesn't produce 1.0 in very rare cases. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2914825447/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2918121029","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106789#issuecomment-2918121029","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106789","id":2918121029,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t7v5F","user":{"login":"EdwardChanCH","id":97891482,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdW0mg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97891482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH","html_url":"https://github.com/EdwardChanCH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-29T03:18:07Z","updated_at":"2025-05-29T03:18:07Z","body":"<img width=\"505\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/68ef6939-635c-4e10-bf41-67baa2961743\" />\n\nChanging the internal calculations of `normalize()` and `length()`  to use `double` instead of `float` did not reduce the inaccuracy. \n\n<img width=\"286\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a8e76761-8207-4944-9118-78318a8f943d\" />\n\n<img width=\"280\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e3dbaad3-1afe-4940-bb02-07b260cb6445\" />\n\nIt is possible to nudge the vector until its length is 1.0, but the performance cost of checking `length()` inside `normalize()` is probably not worth it. \n\nGiven that `Basis::is_orthonormal()` (along with `Basis::is_orthogonal()`, `Basis::is_diagonal()`, and `Basis::is_rotation()`) already exists in the source code, maybe we could instead bind it and add some notes in the official doc? (similar to [Vector3.normalized()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_vector3.html#class-vector3-method-normalized) & [Vector3.is_normalized()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_vector3.html#class-vector3-method-is-normalized))","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2918121029/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]